# Agent-runtime droppings. The daemon runs agents inside each git worktree, and
# they write their own scratch there: `cli.json`/`cursor/cli.json` are
# cursor-agent permission configs (they grant `Shell(**)` and `Shell(rm*)`), and
# `.tmp-run-*.sh`/`.run-tests.sh` are generated runners that hardcode a
# container worktree UUID and `rm -rf node_modules`. A worker's `git add -A`
# swept all of them into commits — #598 landed `cli.json` and `cursor/cli.json`
# on main, #600 carried a third copy, and none of them belong in a checkout.
cli.json
cursor/
.run-tests.sh
.tmp-run-*.sh
